title: The Mark Falls
subtitle: A thousand marks to the dollar.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 8
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.inflation = Math.min(100, Q.inflation + 6);
Q.stability -= 4;
!}

= The Mark Falls

In January a dollar cost under two hundred marks. In August it costs more than a thousand. Since Rathenau's murder no one abroad believes the Republic will last, and the Reichsbank prints whatever the government needs. Prices are now marked up on Monday and again on Thursday.

The men who own things are doing well. Stinnes buys mines, hotels and newspapers with loans he will repay in worthless paper. The workers' wages are fixed for weeks at a time and are worth a third less by payday. In the markets of Berlin and Leipzig, housewives turn on traders they think are hoarding.

The party must say what the workers should do.

- @committees: Build control committees to police prices and hoarding.
- @marches: Lead hunger marches on the town halls.
- @scales: Fight in the unions for wages that rise with prices.

@committees
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Committees of workers and housewives check the shops. Popular, and it builds organisation.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e22_inflation_line = 1;
Q.worker_support += 5;
Q.militancy += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

The first control committees appear in Saxony and Thuringia, then in Berlin. They go from shop to shop with lists of fair prices. Some shopkeepers lower them; some call the police.

@marches
subtitle: The Left's answer. The hungry follow us; so do the police.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0 or ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_inflation_line = 2;
Q.militancy += 8;
Q.repression += 6;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Thousands of unemployed march on the town halls of Chemnitz, Halle and Gelsenkirchen. Some markets are plundered. The police make arrests, and the arrested are mostly ours.

@scales
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's answer. Slow, and it wins respect in the unions.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_union_work == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e22_inflation_line = 3;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Our members in the metalworkers' union move resolution after resolution for a sliding scale of wages. By the autumn some big works pay weekly bonuses tied to the price of bread.
